From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/a733: de, kms: position the primary plane on a black background

[Recipe cut: regenerated: the hunks that touched the removed DE debugfs
knobs are gone.]

MEASURED, 2026-09-26, the 6 GiB board, kernel 6.18.53 with the series before this patch,
a monitor on DP-1 at 1920x1200, no other DRM master (display
manager and kmscon stopped, nothing holding /dev/dri/card*). The documented
playback pipeline

  gst-launch-1.0 filesrc ! qtdemux ! h264parse ! omxh264dec \
    ! videoconvert ! kmssink driver-name=sun60i-kms

fails at preroll with "drmModeSetPlane failed: Invalid argument (22)", and
drm.debug says why:

  [drm:drm_atomic_helper_check_plane_state] Plane must cover entire CRTC
  [drm:drm_rect_debug_print] dst: 1920x1080+0+60
  [drm:drm_rect_debug_print] clip: 1920x1200+0+0
  [drm:drm_atomic_helper_check_planes] [PLANE:33:plane-0] atomic driver check failed

The driver has one plane, the primary, and it could neither move nor scale.
kmssink centres a 1080-line video on the 1200-line mode, which is the most
ordinary thing a video sink does.

WHAT CHANGES

The primary plane becomes positionable (can_position = true), still 1:1. No
register is written that the pipe did not already write. Four words change
their SOURCE from the mode to the plane's clipped destination rectangle:

  register                  address       was          now
  VI0 LAY0_MBSIZE           0x05101004    mode size    dst size
  VI0 OVL_SIZE              0x051010e8    mode size    dst size
  BLD pipe 0 INSIZE         0x05281008    mode size    dst size
  BLD pipe 0 COORD          0x0528100c    0            (y << 16) | x
  (the blender words in all four blender instances, +k*0x400, as before)

Three stay tied to the mode, now on purpose rather than by coincidence: BLD
OUTSIZE (0x0528108c) and the mixer's GLOBAL_SIZE (0x05008108), which is
what the blender hands TCON_TV1, and BKCOLOR (0x05281088 = 0xff000000,
opaque black), which is what fills the screen outside the plane.
LAY0_MBCOOR stays 0: it is the layer's corner inside the channel's own
overlay window, not on the screen, and with one layer the window is the
layer. LAY0_TOP_LADDR becomes the address of the first SHOWN pixel, taken
from the clipped source origin (sun60i_kms_plane_scanout()), because the
layer has no crop register; drm_fb_dma_get_gem_addr() adds the unclipped
src_x/src_y, which is wrong for a plane that hangs over the top or left
edge.

For a plane that covers the mode every one of those words equals what the
mode gave before -- 0x04af077f three times and 0 at 1920x1200 -- and the
address is the same to the byte. A page flip at a fixed rectangle writes
exactly the layer words it always wrote and no blender word: only a plane
whose rectangle changed restages pipe 0's INSIZE and COORD, in the same
batch, after the layer (mainline sun8i's order). fbcon, kmscon and X
program the display engine as before; the enable path writes the same words
in the same order.

Refused, each with a drm.debug line saying why:
  - scaling: min = max = DRM_PLANE_NO_SCALING, unchanged. The channel's
    VSU8 would need a coefficient table that no UM page documents and no
    capture of ours has confirmed; VSU_CTL stays 0.
  - a source origin between two pixels (src.x1/src.y1 & 0xffff): a
    sub-pixel phase is scaling by another name, and truncating it would
    show a picture other than the one asked for.
  - an active CRTC whose primary plane lies wholly off the mode.
    drm_atomic_helper_check_plane_state() calls such a plane "not visible"
    and returns success -- with can_position false as well, so this was
    reachable before -- and .atomic_update then returned early and left the
    PREVIOUS framebuffer scanning. The CRTC check refuses it now, and the
    plane update turns the layer off should it ever be reached, as
    mainline's sun8i layers do.
The display engine's exported seam refuses a rectangle outside the mode
with -EINVAL, so a caller that forgot to clip cannot wrap a 16-bit
coordinate.

WHERE THE VALUES COME FROM

The A733 UM does not document the display engine's registers. V1.00 section
14.3 "Display Engine (DE)", printed pages 641-642 (PDF 662-663), is feature
prose -- output size up to 4096x2048, up to seven alpha-blending channels feeding two
display outputs, four overlay layers per channel, an independent scaler --
and no register table; the V1.00
text extract has zero hits for BLD_, OVL_, BKCOLOR, OUTSIZE, MBSIZE or
blender. So no value here carries a UM line. The register map is the one
this driver already rests on, from the live vendor capture: INSIZE at blender +0x08,
OUTSIZE at +0x8c, MBSIZE at VI +0x04, OVL_SIZE at VI +0xe8, all four
holding 0x04af077f on a live 1920x1200 link. What that capture cannot show,
because its layer is full screen:

  - COORD's half order. The live value is 0, which fits either order.
    Mainline (SUN8I_MIXER_COORD(x, y) = (y) << 16 | (x)) and the vendor's
    field map (de_bld_type.h, bld_coord_reg: xcoord [15:0], ycoord [31:16])
    agree, and the vendor writes it that way (de_bld.c:248-250). Open until
    read back.
  - That INSIZE and OVL_SIZE follow the plane and OUTSIZE the mode.
    Mainline: sun8i_ui_layer.c/sun8i_vi_layer.c write LAYER_SIZE and
    OVL_SIZE from the source, BLEND_ATTR_INSIZE from the destination and
    COORD from dst.x1/y1; sun8i_mixer.c writes OUTSIZE from the mode and
    BKCOLOR black. The vendor: mbsize and win_size from the layer
    (de_ovl.c:440-521), in_size and in_coord from the channel's screen
    window (de_bld.c:229-250, de_channel.c:405-425), out_size from the
    output (de_bld.c:102-131).

WHAT THE VENDOR DOES DIFFERENTLY (allwinner-bsp, branch cubie-aiot-v1.4.8,
drivers/drm/, read for this patch; no code taken)

  - It clips nothing. sunxi_drm_crtc.c:1082-1092 installs no plane
    .atomic_check, de_channel.c:405-408 takes crtc_x/y/w/h and :450-466
    src_x/y/w/h straight from the uAPI, and de_bld.c:248-250 masks x and y
    into 16 bits. A plane hanging over the left edge is written as a
    coordinate near 65535, one over the right edge as a window reaching
    past OUTSIZE. Here the helper clips first, and the clipped source
    offset goes into the scanout address.
  - BKCOLOR = 0 for an RGB output (de_bld.c:128-131), with [31:24] reserved
    in its own field map (de_bld_type.h, bld_bg_color_reg). Ours stays
    mainline's 0xff000000 -- the same RGB -- and what that byte reads back
    is a board reading, not an argument. This corrects sun60i-de.c, which
    said the vendor does not initialise BKCOLOR: it writes 0, and 0 is what
    the live capture holds.
  - For an unscaled RGB layer it clears only the scaler's enable bit and
    leaves the scaler's output size alone (de_channel.c:584-590,
    de_scaler.c:1221-1242) -- the VSU_CTL = 0 this driver writes. That is
    the vendor's own evidence that a smaller unscaled window needs nothing
    more from the VSU; the A523 series' claim that the VSU is never
    bypassed is what the test boot below can falsify.
  - It delivers every write through the RCQ, which latches at frame start,
    so a move never shows a half-written window. Ours is direct MMIO like
    every other datapath write in this driver: a move can show one frame in
    which the channel and the blender disagree about the window. Stage 3's
    line-window guard is where that belongs, and sun60i_de_kms_scanout()
    says so.

VERIFIED BEFORE THE BOARD

  - apply-patches: every series entry at --fuzz=0 on a freshly unpacked
    6.18.53, including arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-behind-iommu1, which
    edits comments in both files after this patch.
  - compile-check green; drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/ rebuilt with W=1: no
    warning from sun60i-de.c or sun60i-kms.c.
  - a full kernel build (localversion -t804), for the test boot below.

HARDWARE-PROVEN on the 6 GiB board, 2026-09-26 (6.18.53-t804 and -t390),
1920x1200 mode, fbcon:
  * a script issuing SETPLANE on plane 33: 1920x1080
    at +0+60 -> MBSIZE, OVL_SIZE, INSIZE 0x0437077F, COORD 0x003C0000;
    1280x720 at +320+240 -> 0x02CF04FF, COORD 0x00F00140; OUTSIZE and
    GLOBAL_SIZE stay 0x04AF077F; closing the card gives fbcon back
    full screen (0x04AF077F, COORD 0). Before this patch the same kmssink
    request failed "Plane must cover entire CRTC", dst 1920x1080+0+60.
  * kmssink 1080p on the 1200 mode runs to EOS with the vblank interrupt working (10 of
    10 with ORC_CODE=backup; with ORC's NEON code 6 of 10 crash in
    videoconvert, unrelated to this patch).
  * X (lightdm) and kmscon unchanged: full-screen words as before, no
    (EE) in Xorg.0.log.
  * BKCOLOR reads back 0x00000000 after the driver's 0xff000000: bits
    [31:24] do not store, as the vendor's field layout says.
  Not run: a human looking at the bars, and the BKCOLOR colour stimulus
  (item 2 below) -- both need eyes at the monitor.

OWED BY THE BOARD (the plan before the run), with the falsifier of each

  1. The kmssink pipeline above, 1080p on the 1920x1200 mode, runs to EOS:
     picture on rows 60..1139, black bars above and below, 1:1, not
     sheared. Falsified by -EINVAL at preroll, a picture at the top, a
     picture that collapses or repeats a column (the VSU claim), or bars
     that are not black.
  2. The bars are BKCOLOR, shown by stimulus: while playing, write
     0x000000ff into BKCOLOR of all four instances (0x05281088 + k*0x400)
     -- the bars turn blue and the video does not; write 0xff000000 back.
  3. Readback while playing: 0x05101004 = 0x051010e8 = 0x05281008 =
     0x0437077f, 0x0528100c = 0x003c0000, 0x05101008 = 0, 0x0528108c =
     0x05008108 = 0x04af077f; 0x05281088 reads 0xff000000 or 0x00000000 and
     says which. debugfs `state` prints "1920x1080 at +0+60" as the layer.
  4. After EOS fbcon is back full screen: 0x05281008 = 0x04af077f,
     0x0528100c = 0; the console proof passes 16/16; kmscon and the X
     desktop come up and look as before.

Assisted-by: Claude
---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun60i/sun60i-de.c
@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@
 #include <linux/seq_file.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_modes.h>
+#include <drm/drm_rect.h>
 
 #include "sun60i-display.h"
 #include "sun60i-kms.h"
@@ -326,6 +327,7 @@
 /* Values. */
 #define DE_VERSION_A733			0x03520100
 #define DE_SIZE(w, h)			((((h) - 1) << 16) | ((w) - 1))
+#define DE_COORD(x, y)			(((y) << 16) | (x))
 #define DE2TCON_MUX_LIVE		0x0000fff5
 #define BLD_COLOR_BLACK			0xff000000
 #define BLD_MODE_SRCOVER		0x03010301
@@ -434,6 +436,14 @@ struct sun60i_de {
 	 */
 	bool				kms_owned;
 	struct drm_display_mode		mode;
+	/*
+	 * Where the layer lands on the mode, in pixels, clipped to it. The
+	 * layer is fetched at this size and the blender places it at this
+	 * position; nothing scales, so one rectangle describes both. The
+	 * debugfs path always sets it to the whole mode; only a KMS plane
+	 * moves it.
+	 */
+	struct drm_rect			dst;
 
 	dma_addr_t			fb_dma;
 	u32				fb_pitch;
@@ -463,6 +473,33 @@ static u32 sun60i_de_bld(unsigned int instance)
 	return DE_DISP0 + DE_DISP_BLD + instance * DE_BLD_STRIDE;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The layer's rectangle in the two encodings the registers use: a size as
+ * (h - 1, w - 1) and a position as (y, x), each in two 16-bit halves.
+ */
+static u32 sun60i_de_dst_size(const struct sun60i_de *de)
+{
+	return DE_SIZE(drm_rect_width(&de->dst), drm_rect_height(&de->dst));
+}
+
+static u32 sun60i_de_dst_coord(const struct sun60i_de *de)
+{
+	return DE_COORD(de->dst.x1, de->dst.y1);
+}
+
+/*
+ * At least one pixel, and entirely inside the mode. The KMS half clips before
+ * it calls, so this is not a second clip: it is the exported seam refusing a
+ * rectangle that would wrap a 16-bit coordinate or run past BLD_OUTSIZE.
+ */
+static bool sun60i_de_dst_fits(const struct drm_display_mode *mode,
+			       const struct drm_rect *dst)
+{
+	return dst->x1 >= 0 && dst->y1 >= 0 &&
+	       dst->x2 > dst->x1 && dst->y2 > dst->y1 &&
+	       dst->x2 <= mode->hdisplay && dst->y2 <= mode->vdisplay;
+}
+
 /*
  * The one place the device tree's window split exists. Every other offset in
  * this file counts from the DE aperture base, which is what the capture, the
@@ -952,27 +989,51 @@ static void sun60i_de_channel_quiesce(struct sun60i_de *de)
  *   FCOLOR(0)                COMPUTED -- AARRGGBB. Opaque black by default,
  *                            which is mainline's BLEND_COLOR_BLACK and what
  *                            silicon carries.
- *   INSIZE(0), COORD(0)      COMPUTED from the mode -- full screen at the
- *                            origin.
+ *   INSIZE(0)                COMPUTED from de->dst -- the layer's size on the
+ *                            screen, (h - 1, w - 1) like every size here.
+ *   COORD(0)                 COMPUTED from de->dst -- the layer's top-left
+ *                            corner in the mode, y in [31:16] and x in [15:0].
+ *                            Mainline's SUN8I_MIXER_COORD() and the vendor's
+ *                            bld_coord_reg (allwinner-bsp de_bld_type.h) both
+ *                            put the halves that way round; the live link
+ *                            carries 0, which cannot tell them apart.
+ *                            A full-screen plane gives exactly the words the
+ *                            mode gave before planes could move: the mode's
+ *                            size, and 0.
  *   ROUTE        0           COMPUTED -- four bits per pipe, pipe 0 <- channel
  *                            0. The zero is the right answer here, not merely
  *                            an untouched register.
- *   OUTSIZE                  COMPUTED from the mode.
+ *   OUTSIZE                  COMPUTED from the MODE, never from the plane. It
+ *                            is what the blender hands the TCON, and it must
+ *                            match TCON_TV1's raster whatever the plane does.
  *   BLEND_MODE(0) 0x03010301 CARRIED, and honestly so: mainline's own comment
  *                            on this constant is "some still unknown magic
  *                            numbers", and the prior art calls it SRCOVER
  *                            without explaining it either. The A733 carries the
  *                            same word verbatim.
  *
+ * WHAT FILLS THE SCREEN OUTSIDE THE LAYER. Two colours are in play, and on this
+ * pipe both are opaque black. Pipe 0 covers only its window (INSIZE at COORD);
+ * inside it the layer is shown, with the pipe's fill colour behind it because
+ * FC_EN(0) is set, as mainline and the vendor both set it. Outside that window
+ * no pipe contributes and the blender outputs BKCOLOR, up to OUTSIZE. So a
+ * plane smaller than the mode is shown on BKCOLOR, and that is the whole of
+ * what "letterbox" means here: no register beyond these nine is involved.
+ * Which of the two colours paints the bars is a board reading, not a
+ * derivation -- change one of them by hand and watch the bars.
+ *
  * TWO REGISTERS ARE WRITTEN THAT THE LIVE LINK LEAVES AT ZERO, and both are
  * departures this driver owns rather than discovers later. PREMULTIPLY = 0 is
  * the value either way, and is written so that a bootloader cannot leave it set
- * for an XRGB8888 layer that has no alpha to premultiply. BKCOLOR = opaque
- * black is what mainline initialises and the vendor does not; it is invisible
- * behind a full-screen opaque layer, which is exactly why the vendor can do
- * without writing it, and it is the first thing that shows the moment a plane is
- * smaller than the screen. The out-of-tree series later added a patch titled
- * "black blender background" for that reason.
+ * for an XRGB8888 layer that has no alpha to premultiply. BKCOLOR is written
+ * 0xff000000, mainline's BLEND_COLOR_BLACK. ⛔ An earlier version of this
+ * comment said the vendor does not initialise it. It does: an RGB output gets
+ * bg_color = 0 (allwinner-bsp de_bld.c:128-131), which its own field map reads
+ * as RGB [23:0] = black with [31:24] RESERVED (de_bld_type.h,
+ * bld_bg_color_reg), and the live link's 0 matches that write. So the two
+ * values differ only in a byte the vendor calls reserved, and both are black.
+ * The value is kept, because it is what this pipe has always written; what the
+ * top byte reads back is recorded rather than assumed (`state`).
  *
  * BLD_OUTCTL, which mainline places at +0xfc and uses for the interlace bit, is
  * NOT written -- and that is a disagreement rather than an oversight. The A523
@@ -984,7 +1045,7 @@ static void sun60i_de_channel_quiesce(struct sun60i_de *de)
 static void sun60i_de_blender(struct sun60i_de *de)
 {
 	const struct drm_display_mode *mode = &de->mode;
-	u32 size = DE_SIZE(mode->hdisplay, mode->vdisplay);
+	u32 out = DE_SIZE(mode->hdisplay, mode->vdisplay);
 	unsigned int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < DE_BLD_INSTANCES; i++) {
@@ -992,12 +1053,14 @@ static void sun60i_de_blender(struct sun60i_de *de)
 
 		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_FCOLOR(DE_BLD_PIPE),
 				de->background);
-		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_INSIZE(DE_BLD_PIPE), size);
-		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_COORD(DE_BLD_PIPE), 0);
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_INSIZE(DE_BLD_PIPE),
+				sun60i_de_dst_size(de));
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_COORD(DE_BLD_PIPE),
+				sun60i_de_dst_coord(de));
 		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ROUTE, 0);
 		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_PREMULTIPLY, 0);
 		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_BKCOLOR, BLD_COLOR_BLACK);
-		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_OUTSIZE, size);
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_OUTSIZE, out);
 		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_MODE(DE_BLD_PIPE),
 				BLD_MODE_SRCOVER);
 		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_PIPE_CTL,
@@ -1007,10 +1070,47 @@ static void sun60i_de_blender(struct sun60i_de *de)
 }
 
 /*
- * The layer -- six registers that matter, every one COMPUTED from the mode and
- * the framebuffer, and the live link's ATTCTL word decodes completely under
- * them with no residue: 0xff008403 is global alpha 0xff, RGB_MODE set, FBFMT
- * 4 = XRGB8888, alpha mode 01 = layer, EN.
+ * Pipe 0's window alone -- the two blender words a moving plane changes. Every
+ * other blender word depends on the mode or on nothing, and a plane update
+ * that is not a modeset leaves them where sun60i_de_blender() put them.
+ */
+static void sun60i_de_blender_window(struct sun60i_de *de)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < DE_BLD_INSTANCES; i++) {
+		u32 bld = sun60i_de_bld(i);
+
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_INSIZE(DE_BLD_PIPE),
+				sun60i_de_dst_size(de));
+		sun60i_de_stage(de, bld + BLD_ATTR_COORD(DE_BLD_PIPE),
+				sun60i_de_dst_coord(de));
+	}
+}
+
+/*
+ * The layer -- six registers that matter, every one COMPUTED from the layer's
+ * rectangle (de->dst) and the framebuffer, and the live link's ATTCTL word
+ * decodes completely under them with no residue: 0xff008403 is global alpha
+ * 0xff, RGB_MODE set, FBFMT 4 = XRGB8888, alpha mode 01 = layer, EN.
+ *
+ * THREE WORDS DESCRIBE A SIZE OR A POSITION, AND NONE OF THEM IS THE SCREEN.
+ *   MBSIZE    the layer's fetch size -- how many pixels per line and lines.
+ *   MBCOOR    the layer's corner inside the CHANNEL's overlay window, not on
+ *             the screen. One layer per channel makes the window the layer,
+ *             so this is 0 wherever the plane sits; the vendor computes it as
+ *             the layer's offset from the channel's bounding box
+ *             (allwinner-bsp de_channel.c:478-482), 0 for a single layer.
+ *   OVL_SIZE  the overlay window, which is what leaves the channel for the
+ *             blender. With VSU_CTL = 0 nothing rescales it, so it must equal
+ *             the blender's INSIZE -- which it does, both being de->dst's size.
+ * Where the layer lands on the screen is the blender's COORD, and only that.
+ * Scaling would make MBSIZE/OVL_SIZE (the source) differ from INSIZE (the
+ * screen) and needs the VSU -- which is exactly what is not done here.
+ *
+ * The address is the first SHOWN pixel, not the buffer's start: the caller has
+ * already added the source offset of a panned or clipped plane, the way
+ * mainline's sun8i layers add src.x1/src.y1. There is no crop register.
  *
  * The plane-1 and plane-2 pitches and addresses are written as zero rather than
  * left alone. They are unused for a packed RGB format and the live link has
@@ -1070,9 +1170,8 @@ static void sun60i_de_blender(struct sun60i_de *de)
  */
 static void sun60i_de_layer(struct sun60i_de *de)
 {
-	const struct drm_display_mode *mode = &de->mode;
 	u32 ovl = sun60i_de_chn(DE_VI0_SLOT) + DE_CHN_OVL;
-	u32 size = DE_SIZE(mode->hdisplay, mode->vdisplay);
+	u32 size = sun60i_de_dst_size(de);
 	unsigned int plane;
 
 	for (plane = 1; plane < OVL_VI_PLANES; plane++) {
@@ -1127,13 +1226,20 @@ static int sun60i_de_layer_disable(struct sun60i_de *de)
  * flag should say after a commit that did not land is a question no backend
  * in this tree can yet pose, and inventing an answer here would change a path
  * silicon has walked.
+ *
+ * @moved restages pipe 0's window in the same batch, after the layer -- the
+ * order mainline's sun8i layers write them in (layer and overlay size, then
+ * blender coordinate and size). Only a plane whose rectangle changed passes
+ * it, so a page flip at a fixed position writes exactly what it always wrote.
  */
-static int sun60i_de_layer_enable(struct sun60i_de *de)
+static int sun60i_de_layer_enable(struct sun60i_de *de, bool moved)
 {
 	int ret;
 
 	de->commit->begin(de);
 	sun60i_de_layer(de);
+	if (moved)
+		sun60i_de_blender_window(de);
 	ret = de->commit->arm(de);
 	de->layer_on = true;
 
@@ -1321,6 +1427,7 @@ static int sun60i_de_state_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 		{ "bld0 PIPE_CTL",	bld + BLD_PIPE_CTL },
 		{ "bld0 FCOLOR0",	bld + BLD_ATTR_FCOLOR(DE_BLD_PIPE) },
 		{ "bld0 INSIZE0",	bld + BLD_ATTR_INSIZE(DE_BLD_PIPE) },
+		{ "bld0 COORD0",	bld + BLD_ATTR_COORD(DE_BLD_PIPE) },
 		{ "bld0 ROUTE",		bld + BLD_ROUTE },
 		{ "bld0 BKCOLOR",	bld + BLD_BKCOLOR },
 		{ "bld0 OUTSIZE",	bld + BLD_OUTSIZE },
@@ -1348,6 +1455,9 @@ static int sun60i_de_state_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 	seq_printf(s, "module clock   : %lu Hz\n", clk_get_rate(de->mod_clk));
 	seq_printf(s, "scanout        : %pad, pitch %u, XRGB8888\n",
 		   &de->fb_dma, de->fb_pitch);
+	seq_printf(s, "layer          : %dx%d at +%d+%d on the mode, unscaled\n",
+		   drm_rect_width(&de->dst), drm_rect_height(&de->dst),
+		   de->dst.x1, de->dst.y1);
 	seq_printf(s, "address kind   : %s\n",
 		   device_iommu_mapped(de->dev) ?
 		   "IOVA (behind an IOMMU) -- NOT comparable with a vendor capture" :
@@ -1373,6 +1483,8 @@ static int sun60i_de_state_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 		   de->cold_version, de->cold_ccsc, de->cold_vsu,
 		   de->cold_tfbd);
 
